From f9425fbc5693546857902b275e3acc5b98ba8d78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:38:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] commands: new run and settings pages

The run page was a server template made for a wide screen: three boxes
in a row, the command line and its arguments squeezed, the result in a
block at the end of the page with no line wrapping, ESC codes shown as
garbage, nothing while a command ran.

Run page (view commands/dashboard):
- cards in a grid that turns into one column on a phone; the name, the
  description in small type, the command shortened to two lines (tap to
  show all), the argument field with a hint and a default value, Enter
  runs the command;
- search by name, description and command; groups with headings that
  fold and stay folded;
- the state on every card: running with its time, done, exit code,
  stopped, time limit, output limit;
- the output window: the output as it comes, colors of the terminal
  (16, 256 and RGB), progress lines redrawn with \r, wrapping of long
  lines on or off, following the end, Stop, Copy (also over http),
  Save (the whole output as a file), Run again. A command keeps running
  when the window or the page is closed and can be opened again;
- confirmation before commands marked so; Download and the public link
  as before.

Settings page (view commands/config): the rows can be dragged (also by
touch) to change the order; new options in the edit dialog: description,
group, argument hint, default arguments, ask before running, time
limit. The command is edited in a monospaced field of several lines.
The UCI options name, description, command, param and public are the
same as in LuCI master.

Checked in Chromium with luci-base 25.12, themes bootstrap and
proton2025, 1280 and 390 pixels wide: 22 checks of the run page (run
with arguments, \r and colors, 3000 lines, stop, reload of the page
during a run, confirmation, wrapping, copy, public link, no horizontal
scroll on a phone), a 9 MB output (8 MiB kept, the page shows the last
1.5 million characters, Save gives all 8 MiB), the settings page with
its edit dialog; no errors in the console.

